## Android lifecycle events in a Kanzi application[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/android/android-appfw.html#android-lifecycle-events-in-a-k-application "Link to this heading")
The Android lifecycle events set how your Kanzi application behaves when the activity state changes. Each event maps to an Android activity callback method. A Kanzi application uses these lifecycle events:
  * `Lifecycle.Event.ON_CREATE`

```
// Load the native library that provides Kanzi functionality,
// initialize the context, and assign the KanziView for rendering.
// This function calls the KanziNativeLibrary.createApplication() function,
// which loads the Kanzi project.
KanziView.createNativeApplication();

```
Copy to clipboard
  * `Lifecycle.Event.ON_DESTROY`

```
// Halt and destroy the Kanzi application.
// This function calls the KanziNativeLibrary.haltApplication() and
// KanziNativeLibrary.destroyApplication() functions.
KanziView.destroyNativeApplication();

```
Copy to clipboard
  * `SurfaceHolder.Callback.surfaceCreated` (`KanziView.surfaceCreated[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-appfw-android-api/a00033.html#ad3194e816beba22527f4a15586928c5c)`)

```
// When the application surface is created, run the Kanzi application.
KanziNativeLibrary.runApplication(holder.getSurface());

```
Copy to clipboard
  * `SurfaceHolder.Callback.surfaceDestroyed` (`KanziView.surfaceDestroyed[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-appfw-android-api/a00033.html#a036e6292a09150ebcccce5737cccba99)`)

```
// When the Kanzi application surface is destroyed, pause rendering.
KanziNativeLibrary.haltApplication();

```
Copy to clipboard
  * `SurfaceHolder.Callback.surfaceChanged` (`KanziView.surfaceChanged[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-appfw-android-api/a00033.html#a09073e032d95e25578c48c49fa847202)`)

```
// When the format or size of the Kanzi application surface changes,
// resize the application surface.
// @param width: The new width of the surface.
// @param height: The new height of the surface.
KanziNativeLibrary.resizeEvent(width, height);

```
Copy to clipboard


Kanzi does not use the `LifeCycle.Event.ON_PAUSE` and `Lifecycle.Event.ON_RESUME` events because they do not tell whether the application surface is ready for rendering. To pause and resume rendering, `KanziView[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-appfw-android-api/a00033.html)` uses these functions:
  * `SurfaceHolder.Callback.surfaceCreated` (`KanziView.surfaceCreated[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-appfw-android-api/a00033.html#ad3194e816beba22527f4a15586928c5c)`)
