## Managing instance lifetime[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/java/using-java.html#managing-instance-lifetime "Link to this heading")
The `ObjectRef[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02659.html)` type enables shared ownership of an instance of `KanziObject[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02475.html)` derived type between the native backend and Java `ObjectRef[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02659.html)` instances. When all `ObjectRef[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02659.html)` instances are closed and no native references exist, the object is reclaimed. If application code attempts to access the object in this state, Kanzi throws a `StaleObjectException[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02779.html)`. To prevent this, maintain an `ObjectRef[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02659.html)` instance for the objects that you use.
Although `ObjectRef[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02659.html)` instances are automatically garbage collected, to have predictable memory consumption, you can manually close such instances.
Java

```
// Create an EmptyNode2D node.
ObjectRef<EmptyNode2D> nodeRef = EmptyNode2D.create(domain, "My Empty Node");

// Access the EmptyNode2D instance from within the ObjectRef.
EmptyNode2D node = nodeRef.get();

// Use the node.

// Close the ObjectRef.
nodeRef.close();

// If you try to access the node variable after closing its ObjectRef,
// Kanzi throws a StaleObjectException.
node.setName("New Name");

```
Copy to clipboard
Kotlin

```
// Create an EmptyNode2D node.
val nodeRef = EmptyNode2D.create(domain, "My Empty Node")

// Access the EmptyNode2D instance from within the ObjectRef.
val node = nodeRef.get()

// Use the node.

// Close the ObjectRef.
nodeRef.close()

// If you try to access the node variable after closing its ObjectRef,
// Kanzi throws a StaleObjectException.
node.name = "New Name"

```
Copy to clipboard
You can also associate the lifetime of an `ObjectRef[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02659.html)` instance to a scope using the Java try-with-resources statement or the Kotlin `use` function:
Java

```
// Create an EmptyNode2D node.
try (ObjectRef<EmptyNode2D> nodeRef = EmptyNode2D.create(domain, "My Empty Node"))
{
    // Access the EmptyNode2D instance from within the ObjectRef.
    EmptyNode2D node = nodeRef.get();

    // Use the node.

    // Kanzi automatically closes the nodeRef at the end of the try block scope.
}

```
