## Creating a native Kanzi Engine plugin manually[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/creating-kanzi-engine-plugins.html#creating-a-native-kr-plugin-manually "Link to this heading")
To create a native Kanzi Engine plugin manually:
  1. In the New tab of the Quick Start window select the Application project template, to create a new project with C++ application.
![../../_images/kanzi-engine-plugin-new-project.png](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/_images/kanzi-engine-plugin-new-project.png)
  2. In File Explorer in the `<ProjectName>/Application` directory, create the `plugin/src` directory.
  3. Add to the `<ProjectName>/Application/plugin/src` directory the file where you add the `createModule`, `deleteModule`, and `Module::getMetaclassesOverride[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a15126.html#ad0452c20a34442086454a8751ea27ae3)` functions, and register all metaclasses that you implement in the plugin.
The plugin uses these functions to get the list of functions, metaclasses, and the component inside the DLL. It uses them to register these to Kanzi Engine.
For example, name that file `my_kanzi_engine_plugin.cpp`.

```
#include <kanzi/core/module/module.hpp>
extern "C"
{
    MY_KANZI_ENGINE_PLUGIN_API kanzi::Module* createModule(uint32_t kanziVersionMajor, uint32_t kanziVersionMinor);
}
class MY_KANZI_ENGINE_PLUGIN_API MyKanziEnginePluginModule: public kanzi::Module
{
    MetaclassContainer getMetaclassesOverride() override;
};
