## Setting the default value of a property type[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/configuring-custom-java-components-for-kanzi.html#setting-the-default-value-of-a-property-type "Link to this heading")
In a custom node you can set the default value of any property type that is defined in the node on which you base your node.
For example, if your node inherits from the `Node2D[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a02627.html)` class, to set the default value of the `metadata.NodeMetadata.OpacityProperty[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-java-api/a04479.html#a3aeedc06e1750f4cf9e056d50bdf56c2)` property type to `0.44`, in the `makeEditorInfo` of your node:
